Rodman rule has been revised but the fight to keep stars in the NWSL goes o=
n


Gone are the eight criteria to be a High Impact Player so clubs can spend t=
heir money on whomever they want =E2=80=93 and the solution makes sense


The rule was informally named after Washington Spirit=E2=80=99s Trinity Rod=
man (left) following her protracted contract saga. Photograph: Jay Biggerst=
aff/NWSL/Getty Images


Megan Swanick


When Washington plays Chicago this Sunday in DC, =E2=80=9CRowdy Audi=E2=80=
=9D will probably be full. It will also be full when the post-season starts=
, should they lock up their top-four position with a positive result on Dec=
ision Day. Equipped with an accessible stadium in a big city, a proud fanba=
se and a formidable roster rife with players qualifying for the High Impact=
 Player (HIP) rule=E2=80=99s initial criteria (including Trinity Rodman, wh=
o gave the rule its moniker), the Spirit hold sway in the attendance charts=
.

But starting next season, everyone on the Spirit
https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTN=
tZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgrVZwi573h5aJedUKhFfwEmyhFprIKcaMeG2=
lYpVI9gZ42fWfW0fsygJHPKeAjc6oGNX1ME8wzWwkNkWzIJiOdF57HzHbD-eW5eN3GXPW-mSGui=
6AIoSDcT6N7SgyU_o88Bfew--R00nMPw7GOLJAT3NG9qO00zyJ7hTsRsrHqKAz2pBbjuENYsEUt=
VywIsX0c-vybI3ddZmDJlb-sQHOugFF6I87Syi6IYQzKO1_UYbz0xn2jgQcMDf_kaKNvbvE/4ve=
/YNg2DqYdTUuyH5sucWty2Q/t0/h001.m4fasaG6_7wM5CRolV1kbjArCmcMHwJiSpixxAPvjfc
will qualify for the =E2=80=9CRodman Rule=E2=80=9D
. So will every player in NWSL. Announced Friday, NWSL settled a grievance =
with the league=E2=80=99s Players Association, who argued that the initial =
criteria violated federal labor law.

Admittedly, when the new policy arrived on the scene last winter, it appear=
ed half-baked, a somewhat frantic attempt to keep Rodman from floating acro=
ss the Atlantic and doing something terrible, like playing for Michele Kang=
=E2=80=99s London City Lionesses instead of Michele Kang=E2=80=99s Washingt=
on Spirit.

A rule was born to prevent that. It allocated added funds beyond the salary=
 cap for players who met league-set criteria that clearly prioritized inter=
national name recognition in a global market. Qualifying players needed to =
meet one of eight categories including SportsPro Media=E2=80=99s top 150 Mo=
st Marketable Athletes (only Alessia Russo and Aitana Bonmat=C3=AD placed i=
n 2026, though 16 female football players did in 2025, including three in t=
he NWSL at the time =E2=80=93 Trinity Rodman, Sophia Wilson and Marta, in t=
hat order). It also included ESPN=E2=80=99s Top 50,
https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTN=
tZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEDom6Up7NBgS48fUZgZf5ceO-Bfvp-VHe3PDtb5mZUQQ-mEahIB-GXmRfP=
L0zNnc51hbTkHUwVqh4alpMRS2cG9EAuYufyu6yer66mmP15mCWJJ_7MQyHoiDs6iU3Tq0soxK9=
4FfUhfGV6RznrR8wPTBOklma6SE47DPFpNslvewh8cd2HRjVfp3Fn73kYizWcVModvgL9q4-Uv1=
RjxSlyvD8MxG_IwReHrOv7Vm3uSL2myghSYfAhoBNXY04icGKBoOwNL3lA80wu6XPe8bdn2Rjpw=
aAdpz4DC6VuNeayx_Q/4ve/YNg2DqYdTUuyH5sucWty2Q/t1/h001.Pnn2X7hOUJR-wMMnHC1Qk=
cmBUCF9q0GVUJTMPkl6abk
the Guardian=E2=80=99s top 100
, top minutes on the US national team, the Ballon d=E2=80=99Or=E2=80=99s 30=
-player list, or NWSL=E2=80=99s MVP and Best XI awards.

Some measure of umbrage followed, as invested onlookers argued for a simple=
r solution: just raise the salary cap. And perhaps they should, but keeping=
 an American-style sports league competitive in a global football landscape=
 is less straightforward. The looming spectre of Europe=E2=80=99s super-tea=
ms, who have attracted key members of the USWNT starting XI, is ever presen=
t, waiting to take Croix Bethune away for the right amount of money. No dou=
bt, the NWSL=E2=80=99s appeal is evident in its expansion and growth, in th=
e success of its spine of stateside stalwarts, in its rapidly expanding ded=
icated facilities, and in the international talents such as Esme Morgan or =
Ann-Katrin Berger that choose to sharpen their skills in the US.

However, the domestic sporting culture of the NWSL is somewhat at odds, in =
some ways a disadvantage, when it comes to maintaining its margins, with a =
stand-alone team structure in a parity-driven league, while competing for i=
nternational glory with teams such as Chelsea, Lyon or Barcelona, who spend=
 three times or more the amount that some NWSL teams do. While competing fo=
r status as the world=E2=80=99s go-to destination, for players and fans, gl=
ory hunting and name recognition do matter.

Just look at the Ballon d=E2=80=99Or: Barcelona=E2=80=99s women took all bu=
t one of the awards available to them, though Alexia Putellas, who
https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTN=
tZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgfixB8L8oyfwfaY5z-TlkJ0fQOEY3X-xfywO=
zWXdCv1IJz5GM6gs9ERIw1zpJk0JbHWms-qtos-m4bIUTXBOrJI1DBY4MBs4QUD0aMeVf43pQwb=
YZ9KMMyCd_dF6ono2TwPHpz0Nioilg-S1tjvBB7WI39ycdvEI7S0IBFjypQhRYIV4aOlFNxOQkx=
G-AiLHkBUpC0nqDBhBXlEXlvjCHeCwRe1oAaApByrKcPT84DOZMOwj5U8dghR03H3BSWvDc5rwi=
wE3VoITOfCbGEieqrqReaXnuL2Sv2_8K8rZ2lUdIBpy-7quju16kRBBQyg9u/4ve/YNg2DqYdTU=
uyH5sucWty2Q/t2/h001.gd57YbBnLj9R1KkMBpXz9uEedMLCp0Dj0JUeMVJiy_Y
collected her third main prize
, now plays in London. That Putellas deserves her trophy is not in dispute,=
 though the inequitable factors contributing to international accolades wer=
e manifest. Putellas starred for two super-teams: Barcelona and Spain. Ewa =
Pajor, Barcelona=E2=80=99s Polish striker, fell just short, perhaps edged o=
ut by only having one super-team to play for.


Alexia Putellas=E2=80=99 performances for two super-teams =E2=80=93 Barcelo=
na and Spain =E2=80=93 offered a fine platform for her to win the Ballon d=
=E2=80=99Or again. Photograph: Tolga Akmen/EPA


Subtly, it seemed, the original criteria for the HIP rule flirted with the =
idea of fostering a super-team in the US. Prior to the update, there was no=
 cap on the number of players who could access the extra million if the sal=
ary cap was already met. For a team such as Kang=E2=80=99s in Washington, t=
he door felt open, possibly, to building a team even more ready to contend =
with the heavy spenders in Europe (including those also funded by Kang), an=
d the international accolades that go with it. If a NWSL player lifted the =
NWSL trophy, helped win January=E2=80=99s inaugural Club World Cup, then pe=
rformed well at the World Cup, could a second NWSL (active) player win the =
Ballon d=E2=80=99Or?

The structure of the HIP rule remains in place. Teams that have met 2027=E2=
=80=99s salary cap of $4.4m (=C2=A33.3m) in 2027 can spend an additional $1=
.257m (as reported by ESPN) on a player. The post-grievance difference is t=
hat teams can spend that additional sum on
any
player. Gone are the stipulations mandating adherence to that eight-criteri=
a list of global recognition.

The change is a win for players that did not meet it, which includes elite =
players who fell short in previous seasons (such as Ashley Sanchez) or star=
 players with long-lasting or recurring injuries (Catarina Macario). It giv=
es the NWSL=E2=80=99s individual teams the autonomy to decide which players=
 are worthy, based on whatever criteria they see fit. And, with a cap on th=
e number of players that can access it, it gives cash-strapped teams the th=
eoretical ability to rein in teams with already-stacked rosters.

But the spirit of NWSL=E2=80=99s original criteria has more merit than many=
 suggest. The NWSL is responsible for securing overhead issues such as an i=
mproved media rights deal, marketing marquee names to broadcasters, ensurin=
g the league is seen as the go-to destination before a World Cup and perfor=
ming well in global cup competitions such as the Concacaf W Champions Cup (=
Mexico=E2=80=99s Club Am=C3=A9rica prevailed in the most recent final) or t=
he upcoming Club World Cup. With that in mind =E2=80=93 plus the ever-press=
ing desire to keep USWNT players in the US =E2=80=93 the original HIP crite=
ria had its eye on awarding stardom as it=E2=80=99s seen in the global mark=
et.

Stardom is imprecise. It=E2=80=99s hard to measure, but impossible to miss.=
 Rodman did not make the Ballon d=E2=80=99Or shortlist and is not leading t=
he Golden Boot race. But Rodman and her closest national team peers (includ=
ing
