<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Arsenal are three points clear <a href=3D"=
https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTN=
tZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHED-7nBbyfP2xYdGcaDqHcyJODXR-pf25q4u8URzLCwB8nl4qUfEpy1Yw2n=
YWaLxeLY8I11sHTpG7sFt6x2o2FgnQfG2RSbb9qIYRwa2z0KbQYz7XZX_1wwcyrmd4WtNPXEr_A=
lX11AuOqb0RjI2h_s9JObTVSqe4WmzY-bfClzpMDtMszLPRQ0GtFQePFj3NLYoCQtSxgHWrihap=
TqyDIVvVE7uUV8qD60onJ9hO-TcvA/4ve/YNg2DqYdTUuyH5sucWty2Q/h9/h001.7lQpvzmloY=
50zRXv8iT9HofvZWw8jT2XQRr4xvFgFJA" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">at the top of =
the Premier League table</a>. But given the team in second are Manchester C=
ity, who are likely to be facing at the very least a <a href=3D"https://abl=
ink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgsz=
cCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgLZWnuIPYdLNOd465HzgluS_vF4SDb7eE20Ms77vG3Mcx8h=
ElWQW2W85ts3LIpbcug79NG-nMIj5pxNhH5T8gW4BOrn_95RvTPhmcgH-9YZrL6GA5wwqI0aZDw=
Bnng1UQZDih4DC2z2lmCw2HHW4wuLQ6HMXlF9rtgeI9mUQYdY80wtmwMryAwRfbWPSPc_fXd4kH=
Nx7J3py7_tP-PeWff6u1LsCN3XirJA92KaqznHhWX_PzIi6B4UN1BPihSphFgfh7rLbc2Ct9ghf=
ZKd76JD9HwtQKLlQQlBV3HBOOd6o/4ve/YNg2DqYdTUuyH5sucWty2Q/h10/h001.o1tU87tRTw=
_CAbp6N2EQ5TXY9avwXv4HJ41JPHghjPY" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">major points d=
eduction</a>, perhaps more significant is that they are five clear of Brigh=
ton in third. The season of domination that many anticipated from the champ=
ions appears to be coming to pass.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Liverpool challenged them on Sunday. There=
 was a 20-minute spell before half-time when they swarmed all over Arsenal,=
 and Anfield felt at least like it did in the golden years of J=C3=BCrgen K=
lopp, when it buzzed with an energy that could overwhelm visitors. But Arse=
nal got through that, reset at half-time, and navigated the second half wit=
h relative comfort. For the second league game running, they denied Liverpo=
ol a shot on target.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">If there is a lesson, it is that Liverpool=
, like Brighton, demonstrated that a very aggressive press can unsettle Ars=
enal. But then, a very aggressive press can unsettle anybody. In <a href=3D=
"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyT=
NtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPg3RJ44Fso9uMyQxe28Dp72VUa-frxnpRGmJ=
WyK1RXsYXS15zy0MHbmkayPdyx1qmO7rJKczGBVePBiNdnQvwhZ2jQgC3i6MnZN7mbP7HI3nxW_=
wMx55P4jAerWE-5EQWP6k58bxAPXkYo2aWezDEHBqtWR4YXNGQnxYdb_fSZRvi-D-CEWEnXbIS_=
3XJXH5SwF3WjJZvU64DeLXDqhJJyhpD4r-Ool8zilEqn1U1SNUBte5bBydDXQRLNB4Q0ySky3gR=
cWaILF2wAv1D0PeUaXQ/4ve/YNg2DqYdTUuyH5sucWty2Q/h11/h001.G3UCFzXYbhJbQOjmpy4=
sHCr768m1ly837D4N9WoL1Jw" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">Arsenal=E2=80=99s loss =
at Brighton</a>, Pascal Gross and Charalampos Kostoulas took difficult oppo=
rtunities; at Anfield Liverpool were denied what should surely have been a =
penalty when Jurri=C3=ABn Timber tugged Alexander Isak=E2=80=99s shirt =E2=
=80=93 another bad moment for VAR, in that the no-call essentially mandated=
 players to go down and highlight contact. Later, Alexis Mac Allister put a=
 free header over. That was the difference, and this Arsenal team will not =
give opponents many chances. They are good at closing games out. Ezri Konsa=
 in particular was outstanding on Sunday.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">They also have a strong bench. The policy =
has been to make the squad deeper rather than adding the very highest quali=
ty =E2=80=93 which is why the links with Vin=C3=ADcius J=C3=BAnior over the=
 summer were so unexpected. That has frustrated some, but it has been succe=
ssful. Arsenal on Sunday could bring on Myles Lewis-Skelly, Piero Hincapi=
=C3=A9, Viktor Gy=C3=B6keres and Mikel Merino to protect their lead with ve=
ry little diminution of quality. But it=E2=80=99s not just on a man-to-man =
level that Liverpool=E2=80=99s options suffer by comparison; their changes =
upset the balance. They never really had control of the game once Dominik S=
zoboszlai had come on for Trey Nyoni.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">It=E2=80=99s been a recurring feature of t=
his season that Arsenal turn half-time draws into full-time wins =E2=80=93 =
it=E2=80=99s already happened seven times. Winning individual games, though=
, is only part of it; a deeper squad means there can be more rotation, whic=
h should help prevent fatigue as the season goes on, as well as providing a=
dditional cover when injuries do occur. That said, their depth was not suff=
icient <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkL=
MEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgB6Yo-rBlAmOLV78P7=
3wq-NSaBDI2pwmYLT_YM02dExTJnWYr3ocvoxKNlvOEEpyR-O0zRFptuuegq9kIiVBJORMFRmrb=
F1i9OZC_pXLpSxe2HUBRCDJ7o3f_4axnJLJgLp1q7J3TbTWcnapftX7_pvoM5CRCiKUXkAYeR3a=
mN8CAz4Phyap9x4USK-sba7GDUCj0-0Rp3krOy6lfXVEUgvFjqz4JHa6K2EJ7CZnSy013RBqyzr=
6JvyjXKkWTEjwEQLYoF8I9GqP4wYVdI5F1q19nRrsyj8AwODLmw1E9BFk/4ve/YNg2DqYdTUuyH=
5sucWty2Q/h12/h001.lGLtFc71_mFrR5wFVu_e5ziJOpI8zvD8aS10dNQzgmQ" style=3D"co=
lor: #0077B6;">to get them past Fleetwood</a> in the Carabao Cup last week,=
 although they will face few games in conditions as challenging as those on=
 the Lancashire coast.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">There are still three-quarters of the seas=
on to go, and Arsenal were in a similarly commanding position at this stage=
 last season, four points clear of second-placed Bournemouth after nine gam=
es. The expectation then was for a procession that didn=E2=80=99t materiali=
se and looked, amid a spring wobble, to have gone awry. Then as now the fee=
ling was not merely that Arsenal were very good, but that none of their riv=
als looked especially threatening.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">But this season they have the memory of wi=
nning the title; the insecurity of three successive second-place finishes s=
hould be lessened. There is a resilience to them that has already brought a=
 first win at Anfield since 2012 and a victory at Nottingham Forest after s=
uccessive goalless draws at the City Ground. They=E2=80=99re picking up poi=
nts at grounds where they=E2=80=99ve stumbled.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Last season, City were more resilient than=
 had been anticipated. It may be a different story this time, and not just =
because of the potential for a savage points deduction. After seven straigh=
t wins they have lost successive league games to Aston Villa and Brighton, =
but the vulnerabilities that have been exposed had been apparent earlier in=
 the season: a high defensive line that can be exploited. Liverpool are sta=
rting to coalesce under Andoni Iraola but they haven=E2=80=99t clicked quit=
e yet and are, anyway, nine points adrift. Chelsea are a point better off b=
ut still a work in progress. Brighton have probably been the best other sid=
e, but they don=E2=80=99t have the depth to be considered a title challenge=
r.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Sunday made clear what was already widely =
suspected: Arsenal are the best team in the league by some margin. It=E2=80=
=99s not just their depth, their cohesion and the wide variety of situation=
s from which they can score goals, it=E2=80=99s that they now have belief a=
nd are picking up points at places where they have often failed in the past=
. And if they do build up a substantial lead by Easter, that could be hugel=
y beneficial to their European challenge, which remains the one unconquered=
 frontier.</p>
