uTt57w3CGsDt9jbES_Kr8yaMCRkVFY" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">by a red card rev=
ersal scandal</a>, and just as it seemed a summer move away from Monaco cou=
ld get his career on track, he broke off a possible transfer to Everton aft=
er a lengthy visit to the training grounds.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">While many expected that Balogun would get=
 his move in January, to the Premier League or elsewhere, Monaco have under=
standably prepared for life without him. New manager Filipe Luis continues =
to prefer Paris Brunner to the US international, giving the 20-year-old amp=
le time to tap into his vast potential. Balogun=E2=80=99s opportunities to =
turn the page have been limited.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">On Sunday, though, at least in statistical=
 terms, Balogun took the first steps toward a post-2026 future, scoring the=
 lone goal in a losing effort as Monaco fell 3-1 to Paris FC.</p>
