<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Even by the standards of the Britannia Sta=
dium, it was a windy day when Stoke City met Southampton in a Premier Leagu=
e game on 2 November 2013. Southampton kicked off, and promptly lost the ba=
ll, with the Stoke left-back Erik Pieters nudging it back to his goalkeeper=
, Asmir Begovi=C4=87. The Bosnian was standing on the edge of his six-yard =
box. He sized up the ball rolling towards him and advanced about three yard=
s towards it, launching it long downfield. The ball soared, bouncing back t=
o earth about 25 yards from the Southampton goal. A little drizzle had star=
ted to fall and it was perhaps that, combined with the pre-match sprinklers=
 that caused the ball to skip over Artur Boruc in the Southampton goal. The=
 Polish keeper turned, stumbling slightly and watched in horror as the ball=
 bounced just in front of the line and carried on into the net: <a href=3D"=
https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IR-Mf=
wplWHIOxat_BLmbIftdjeP0gygUoxl82DFqoDKRaiHm2In0zBsL2d-E5-RifSpEITU9GypQ2s0C=
J9bn3cVFdEsqpfNwn0ePaMcI0KwEt4PqPOSz9YBD7Mzjfsnkecc0NLHAKF7HR0kO8Bn8n5i4SM_=
BCxrWQ8f2DDOGeq_DghJpEmb4Y7aH4yeLix2CHXuCCY47-iYhrZ_gmRmO6EKWmBACvVO4LkvsPK=
RQAv5AUOvfrbdbe3xIyCLNvZORfNg/4ve/YNg2DqYdTUuyH5sucWty2Q/h16/h001.fJvkqCnTo=
y1bdR_G_zF67r3kSakbeaLlhrTs-WM5p1Q" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">a goal after =
13 seconds</a>. The distance was officially given as 97 metres, just beatin=
g a Tim Howard goal as the longest-range strike in Premier League history.<=
/p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Jay Rodriguez headed in a James Ward-Prows=
e delivery to level things three minutes before the break and the game ende=
d 1-1. Stoke finished the season ninth with Southampton a place above them.=
</p>
